{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1113080-focused-mage-sight-or-supernals-in-your-scrutiny","id":1113080,"title":"Focused Mage Sight, or Supernals in Your Scrutiny","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-07T20:44:38-07:00","id":1113080,"title":"Focused Mage Sight, or Supernals in Your Scrutiny","content":"First off, this isn't about disliking Mage Sight. I like it, your own feelings are respected but I'm looking for what people did with or plan on doing with it.<br /> <br /> While performing a Scrutiny, if you get a Dramatic Failure, no successes are accrued. However, 'If the player has already made a number of rolls equal to the unmodified dice pool, a Supernal entity of the mage\u2019s Path takes note of the mage and may affect him with its powers as long as he maintains his Mage Sight.'<br /> <br /> What are these Supernal entities going to want to do? My only experience with them throughout the books involves mages summoning them when they want something. What does a Supernal entity do when it takes note of the mage? Is it angry or curious? Does it help or hinder?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T21:15:59-07:00","id":1113091,"title":"","content":"I kind of get the impression it's annoyed since Mage Sight is essentially a brute force method of examining the Supernal. It's the metaphysical equivalent of knocking on the gates of heaven with a battering ram.<br /> <br /> That said, Supernal Entities don't seem to be able to help Mages who can't pass their Trial, so it seems appropriate to me that they would take the opportunity to burden the Mage with their Trial (Probably ramped up somewhat from their standard summoned version) as a way of forcing the Mage to do penance. If you can pass, at least they'll leave you alone (&quot;Helping&quot; by not interfering further), maybe if you pass with flying colors they'll offer their assistance. <br /> <br /> I figure handling it like that rams the idea home that a Mage who insists on trying to stumble forward despite their inadequacy to the task (Breaking Opacity down) is an AoH without necessarily incurring the Wisdom risk and may also be an experiential learning opportunity. <br /> <br /> A particularly clever/hubristic/desperate Mage may even use a Dramatic Failure on Scrutiny on purpose, as an attempt to bypass the usual Summoning rules that carries a risk of catching the attention of the Abyss. They wouldn't get the benefit of targeting their summons to a particular kind of Supernal Entity though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T01:22:44-07:00","id":1113148,"title":"","content":"I can also imagine that Wisdom would play some role. The effects of Wisdom on dice bonuses/penalties for interactions with Astral and Supernal entities seem not to have made it into the core book, however nothing prevents you from using them (or just to roleplay the effects of Wisdom), when you use the Focused Sight. Your Nimbus probably makes much bigger mess if it's uncontrolled.<br /> <br /> See, this is the kind of thing I would love to be explained in SoS. There will apparently be chapter dealing with things like Summoning and Mage Sight (including the differences in how the different Paths perceive the same Arcanum).<br /> <br /> Also, if I remember correctly, there will be a merit that will reflect that you caught attention of a Supernal entity, which will, among other things, allow you to see it in your Mage Sight permanently. I think it's called Supernal Watcher, but I don't know much else about it. <span style=\"font-size:8px\">We would have to ask Dave about spoilers for Supernal beings in SoS.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T08:42:27-07:00","id":1113262,"title":"","content":"This is exactly what happened to my Obrimos player some chapters ago. A mystic-fueled storm was battering Manila, and he decided to use Focused Prime and Forces Sights to analyze the phenomenon. One too many rolls later, he was staring into the Aether, and a cherubim noticed him.<br /> <br /> This was no rosy-cheeked infant with wings mind you, but a living, swirling pillar of flame, Old Testament-style. (The PC's Obsession had to do with angelology) Poor guy lost his eyesight, and is still currently blind in our current chronicle. His reward was an Arcane Beat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4260-terpsichordean","name":"terpsichordean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4260_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T04:31:36-07:00","id":1114107,"title":"","content":"In my chronicle, the player (Obrimos) also failed dramatically his spell along with his scrutiny. Aether was superimposed into his sight as angered winged creatures with long necks that ended into a single eye were hunting him. So they forced him to relieve his Awakening (it was a painful self-immolation) in order to learn and contain his hybris. His casting is significantly more careful now :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6169-shadowjim12","name":"Shadowjim12","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T17:07:48-07:00","id":1114319,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I can't help but think of the Hounds of Tindalos here. Seeing something indescribable that can, in turn, now see you and is now moving towards you and maybe it wants to help you, or eat you, or maybe you wouldn't like its help, but you<br /> Just.<br /> don't. <br /> know.<br /> <br /> If the Mage hasn't dropped their mage sight by that point, they deserve to be eaten. Or something.<br /> <br /> Granted, as described in the original story, the titular Hounds sound more like Abyssal entities, but some of the Anachronisms could be similar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T20:36:51-07:00","id":1114887,"title":"","content":"The way I see it, an eidolon's attention is incomprehensible. You have a fundamental concept that <i>defines</i> some significant aspect of whatever you are examining suddenly paying attention to you. That's some strange stuff.<br /> <br /> There are many ways this could go poorly, from it deciding that it doesn't like you to deciding that it <i>does</i> like you. There are even more ways it could go well or simply oddly. (That could also involve its curiosity, positive, or negative attentions.)<br /> <br /> If the eidolon in question favors the things you are and are doing, it will likely be favorably disposed. If you more strongly represent some oppositional definition, it will more likely dislike you. Forcing a trial on you could be its prelude to doing something nice to you, but that could involve a lot of pain and suffering to gain something you didn't actually want. A spirit removing your vulnerability to injuries caused by weapons as a punishment for something could conceivably happen, say.<br /> <br /> Seems more likely to me that the interaction would usually be really intense and strongly related to the manifestation of that thing. A leadership eidolon might force a character to try to demonstrate leadership, improving their abilities or demonstrating their weaknesses. Alternately, it might make the character review all leadership choices made and run through some theoretical scenarios. It might even remove any concept of the character being a leader from all minds, if displeased, too.<br /> <br /> I figure most should be pretty neutral and involve a sort of weird investigation by the thing, experienced by the mage something like Mage Sight scrutiny. (meaning that they see many things about the symbol in question (whether direct or opposite) respecting their self.)<br /> I kinda like the idea of a parting effect, something like a Brand, from the eidolon in question that marks them as favored or not of that eidolon, should they leave a sufficient impression and sometimes even if not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}